  "worked_solution": "The ratio of the number of books to shelves is $34:2.$ So we start with the ratio $34:2$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{34}{2}\n$$\n\nWe can make a denominator of $1$ by dividing the numerator and denominator by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{34÷2}{2÷2}=\\frac{17}{1}=17\n$$\n\nSo, $34$ books in $2$ shelves $=17$ books per shelf.",
